# `iou-value` Standalone Wire Specification

`iou-value` is the numeric 8-byte prefix of a classic 48-byte issued
`STAmount`. It intentionally omits the 20-byte currency and 20-byte issuer and
is therefore a numeric test-vector format, not a complete ledger amount.

## Bit layout

| Bits | Meaning | Adversarial note |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 63 | Issued-currency discriminator; always 1 | A native amount word is not an IOU value even though it is also eight bytes. |
| 62 | Positive flag | Zero is signless: canonical issued zero is `8000000000000000`. |
| 61..54 | Exponent plus 97 | Canonical exponent range is -96 through +80. |
| 53..0 | Mantissa | Nonzero canonical range is 10^15 through 10^16-1. |

Encoding constructs a valid issued amount with dummy currency/issuer context,
serializes it through `STAmount`, and returns only the first eight bytes.
Decoding requires exactly eight bytes, supplies a valid dummy suffix so the
real `STAmount` parser can enforce its invariants, and returns only the numeric
value. No field header or amount suffix belongs in this standalone codec.

